# DID ANYBODY LOOK? One row per question a document was asked about its own diligence,
# carrying what it answered.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS IS THE ROW THAT MAKES AN EMPTY TABLE READABLE, AND WITHOUT IT AN EMPTY TABLE IS
#    AMBIGUOUS IN THE WORST WAY. A filing with no couplings has either a stack of independent
#    layers or nobody who looked; a fusion with no eliminations has either no double counting
#    or no search for it. Those are opposite claims and the tall table renders them
#    identically. The search element is where the difference lives.
#
# ⭐⭐ AND THE ANSWER DECIDES WHICH ARITHMETIC IS OWED, which is what raises this above
#    bookkeeping. `none` or `notApplicable` on a fusion: the composed figure must equal the
#    sum of its converted parts EXACTLY. `unmeasured`: no equality is owed at all, and a
#    checker reporting one is reporting about nothing.
#
# ⛔ A NULL `answer` IS NOT AN ABSENCE HERE. It means the document actually filed the thing --
#   real couplings, real eliminations -- so the search question is answered by the content.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE TWO MEMBERS ARE FILES, AND THAT IS WHAT MAKES THIS UNION HONEST. Build both arms
#    inline against their base tables and every caller wanting one KIND of search filters on the
#    `looked_for` string this file invented: a union taken back apart by string comparison at
#    every call site, and callers that give up and read the base table instead. A
#    `:union` whose members are not files is a union nobody can compose half of.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings and asrt:Fusion/asrt:eliminations, each with its pm:absent.
SELECT cs.filing, 'couplings between layers' AS looked_for, '(the stack)' AS about,
       cs.answer, cs.note
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) cs
UNION ALL
SELECT es.composition, 'double counting across parts', es.composed_layer,
       es.answer, es.note
FROM (
    :compose(eliminations/searched.sqlc)
) es
